# BigQuery Query Header

Every BigQuery query you write (inline in chat, in a `.sql` file, or staged for someone to run) **must start with a comment line attributing its origin**:

- From a JIRA ticket → `# https://lightspeedhq.atlassian.net/browse/LSR-XXXX` (full URL, not just the key)
- From a Slack discussion → `# slack discussion YYYYY` (use the thread link, date, or channel/thread identifier in place of `YYYYY`)

The header is the **first line**, before any `DECLARE` or `WITH`.

## Examples

<good-example>
```sql
# https://lightspeedhq.atlassian.net/browse/LSR-37887
DECLARE LOOKBACK_DAYS INT64 DEFAULT 1095;

WITH latest_payment_types AS (
  ...
)
SELECT ...
```
</good-example>

<good-example>
```sql
# slack discussion https://lightspeed.slack.com/archives/C0XXXX/p1717430000
SELECT COUNT(*) FROM `ls-data-platform-prd.retail_binlog_row_unified.payment_type_unified` ...
```
</good-example>

<bad-example>
Bare key instead of the full URL:
```sql
# LSR-37887
SELECT ...
```
</bad-example>

<bad-example>
No attribution header — origin of the query is untraceable:
```sql
DECLARE LOOKBACK_DAYS INT64 DEFAULT 1095;
SELECT ...
```
</bad-example>

If the query maps to both a ticket and a discussion, prefer the JIRA URL.
